      "message": "Not familiar with these address specifically, but the rollback regions in helipilot are defined consistently with bloonchipper as:\n\n#define CONFIG_ROLLBACK_OFF (CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_RO_SIZE)\n#define CONFIG_ROLLBACK_SIZE (128 * 1024 * 2) /* 2 blocks of 128KB each */\n\nwhere CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF is 0 and CONFIG_RO_SIZE is (128 * 1024), putting the rollback flash addresses at 20000 and 40000. If the 8000000 offset on top of that is expected in the context of a data access violation, think we are good here. Can anyone confirm or do I need to do more digging?",
